sum='One night in a village, a tired man and his wife are about to sleep when they hear someone digging into their house. The man whispers that a thief must have got past Rama, the village kotwal (policeman). The thief, hiding inside, hears their voices and decides to wait until they fall asleep; he wonders where they keep their money. The clever husband pretends to talk to his wife about naming their future child: “If it is a boy, we will call him Rama.” He says that when the boy is in the house he will call softly, “Rama! Rama!”; if he is in the yard he will call a little louder; and if he is in the street, he will call out very loudly – “RAMA!” The foolish thief thinks it is a silly game and waits. Rama the kotwal hears his name, runs to the house, sees the hole dug by the thief, enters and arrests him: “You’re under arrest.” The couple rejoice – “The plan worked! We’re saved!” By their cleverness they saved themselves from being robbed.',
